---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
Generate UUIDs: random (v4), time-ordered (v7), from a name (v3, v5), or v1, v6

Usage: tw uuid generate [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --v4                Random (the default)
      --v7                Time-ordered: starts with the time, so it sorts by creation
      --v5                From --name in --namespace, with SHA-1
      --v3                From --name in --namespace, with MD5
      --v1                From the time and a random node
      --v6                From the time and a random node, sortable
      --namespace <TEXT>  For v3 and v5: dns, url, oid, x500, or a UUID; dns when left out
      --name <TEXT>       For v3 and v5: the name the UUID is made from
  -n, --count <N>         How many UUIDs to generate
  -u, --upper             Write the hex digits in uppercase
      --json              Write the result as JSON
      --no-newline        Do not end text output with a newline
  -h, --help              Print help
